---
title = "How to check if a file exists"
meta_title = "How to check if a directory exists in Gleam"
subtitle = "using simplifile"
description = "The simplifile package provides file system functionality that works with Gleam on both Erlang and JavaScript"
---

The `simplifile` package provides file-system functions that work on both the
Erlang and JavaScript targets. Add it as a dependency to your package:

```cli
gleam add simplifile
```

Use the [`simplfile.is_file`](https://simplifile.hexdocs.pm/simplifile.html#is_file)
function to check if a file exists at a given path.

```gleam
import simplifile

pub fn main() -> Nil {
  case simplifile.is_file("pokemon_cards.txt") {
    Ok(True) -> todo as "file exists"
    Ok(False) -> todo as "file does not exist"
    Error(_) -> todo as "could not tell if file exists"
  }
}
```

If a directory exists at the path then `is_file` will return `False`.

If the file cannot be checked for any reason, these functions will return a
[`simplifile.FileError`](https://simplifile.hexdocs.pm/simplifile.html#FileError).

::: alert-warning
### Files and web browsers

For security reasons web browsers do not let code directly read and write
files, so if your program runs in browser you will need to use a different
approach.

:::
